WEBVTT

00:00.740 --> 00:02.530
There! There! There!

00:04.070 --> 00:05.690
Oh, there you go.

00:06.850 --> 00:10.530
Look! I can control them pretty well now!

00:10.530 --> 00:14.740
Looks like you've grown awfully 
fond of those tentacles, Maple.

00:14.740 --> 00:18.450
They might be a powerful 
weapon in the next event.

00:18.450 --> 00:23.160
We'll have to find our 
monster partners by then.

00:23.160 --> 00:26.190
Kanade, you said you already 
know what yours will be, right?

00:26.190 --> 00:28.540
Since I mostly provide support for you guys,

00:28.540 --> 00:31.940
I think I'd prefer one that's 
versatile rather than a specialist.

00:31.940 --> 00:34.970
One with good healing power 
would be the best match for me.

00:34.970 --> 00:37.940
I'm working on a pretty 
long quest right now,

00:37.940 --> 00:39.720
so I'm sure I'll find something.

00:39.720 --> 00:42.760
I think I'd like a monster that's 
geared toward production work.

00:42.760 --> 00:46.560
I'm sure not all the monsters are 
just specialized for combat.

00:46.560 --> 00:51.370
Wow, I guess there's a lot to think 
about if you're searching for one.

00:51.370 --> 00:55.880
Normally, yeah. We were both a 
perfect match for these guys,

00:55.880 --> 00:57.280
so we just got lucky.

00:57.670 --> 00:59.330
That's for sure, huh, Syrup?

00:59.330 --> 01:00.240
Turtle!

01:00.240 --> 01:04.490
It'll be easier for us to move together 
once we finish our tame monster hunts.

01:05.050 --> 01:07.920
All right! Let's plan 
to get this done today!

01:08.180 --> 01:10.040
I'm going to look around the town.

01:10.330 --> 01:14.380
I guess I'll do that, too. There 
might be quests available.

01:14.380 --> 01:16.270
Good luck, everyone!

01:16.270 --> 01:17.240
Turtle!

01:19.280 --> 01:28.100
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

02:46.140 --> 02:48.020
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

02:48.620 --> 02:53.380
<b>Maxing Defense </b>and <b>Tame Monsters</b>.

02:50.540 --> 02:54.510
I've checked out the library to 
research monsters that might be good,

02:54.510 --> 02:56.570
but I didn't really get any leads.

02:56.920 --> 03:00.030
Well, I guess I'll just walk around for now.

03:02.900 --> 03:07.260
<i>I've pretty much memorized all 
the players and NPCs here.</i>

03:07.580 --> 03:09.910
<i>I saw that player once before,</i>

03:10.310 --> 03:13.620
<i>and I've seen those two NPCs twice.</i>

03:15.000 --> 03:17.380
<i>Oh, and I know those guys, too.</i>

03:17.380 --> 03:20.720
One full set of healing items...

03:21.230 --> 03:23.910
Is this all the stuff Dread asked us to get?

03:23.910 --> 03:26.550
Now we just gotta get the stuff Drag wanted.

03:26.550 --> 03:29.090
Oh, what a magnificent bouquet!

03:29.090 --> 03:31.230
It's a perfect match for Frederica!

03:31.450 --> 03:33.800
She'll yell at you for wasting the money.

03:33.800 --> 03:36.340
Though if you wanna use 
your own, that's on you.

03:43.270 --> 03:45.370
I've never seen that NPC before.

04:07.590 --> 04:10.280
I was sure I'd find something...

04:11.730 --> 04:12.940
Nothing at all, huh?

04:14.690 --> 04:16.360
Yeah, as if.

04:19.570 --> 04:22.430
This is it. The books are 
arranged differently.

04:24.650 --> 04:26.990
Found it! So that was...

04:26.990 --> 04:28.660
Quest: "Mirror Image"

04:26.990 --> 04:28.660
Conditions for completion:

04:26.990 --> 04:28.660
Defeat the event monster "Mirror Slime"

04:28.660 --> 04:32.160
A Mirror Slime, eh? I like it.

04:34.290 --> 04:38.330
Hm... I get it. "Mirror Image."

04:41.070 --> 04:43.700
I know where I need to go.

04:46.950 --> 04:50.610
Now I just hope it's close to 
the ability I expect it to be.

04:55.620 --> 04:57.690
A dead end...

05:08.070 --> 05:10.780
Found you! [Spell Stash]!

05:21.160 --> 05:25.290
I see. This might take 
longer than I thought.

05:25.720 --> 05:28.680
[Magic Fire Bullet]! [Voice of the Dead]!

05:28.680 --> 05:31.890
[Anti-Sorcery Barrier]! [Robe of Blessing]!

05:34.070 --> 05:37.080
[Anti-Magic]! [Mana Flight]!

05:37.080 --> 05:38.270
[Power Decay]!

05:40.520 --> 05:43.610
I wish I could use that so enthusiastically!

05:43.610 --> 05:45.190
[Firestorm]!

05:45.190 --> 05:46.780
[All Resist]!

05:46.780 --> 05:48.360
[Summon Decoy]!

05:50.740 --> 05:52.010
[Breath of Destruction]!

05:52.010 --> 05:53.450
[Divine Punishment]!

05:53.450 --> 05:55.140
[Gravity Axe]!

06:04.340 --> 06:06.100
Okay, then...

06:06.700 --> 06:12.960
Now I just need to activate 50 spells or 
skills, and it'll become my companion?

06:12.960 --> 06:18.560
Well, the book did say it would transform 
into other creatures in pursuit of knowledge.

06:18.560 --> 06:22.020
It must have a ton of curiosity.

06:22.260 --> 06:25.480
Okay, let's do this in one go. 
Make sure you're watching!

06:31.450 --> 06:32.990
And this finishes it!

06:37.120 --> 06:39.180
Quest complete!

06:39.180 --> 06:41.830
Let's see... Your stats are...

06:41.830 --> 06:43.790
Mirror Slime

06:43.790 --> 06:45.660
It's stronger than I thought.

06:46.230 --> 06:48.760
That was a happy miscalculation.

06:49.330 --> 06:51.810
I think I'll call you "Sou."

06:54.230 --> 06:55.560
Okay, Sou!

06:55.560 --> 06:56.540
[Mimic]!

07:03.220 --> 07:07.400
I see. The strength of the 
skill is half of my own.

07:07.400 --> 07:10.950
But that's good enough. That's 
not its real strength, anyway.

07:11.450 --> 07:14.020
I think we'll make a great team, Sou.

07:20.520 --> 07:21.870
Hmm...

07:22.150 --> 07:25.960
The non-rare monsters seem 
pretty strong, too...

07:25.960 --> 07:29.340
Are there any fit for production work?

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
A Recently Discovered Spirit-Type Monster?

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
Requested by madorisuta-san

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
Must produce a set number of new items
 to complete the quest... 
No one has been able to obtain anything yet
 due to the high difficulty level.

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
5 Responses   Show All

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
Grants-san

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
I checked this out, but when I saw 
that it requires a dragon's scale and some ores, I gave up.

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
Very informative!

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
Comment

07:30.300 --> 07:34.640
Cancel

07:30.730 --> 07:34.130
"A Recently Discovered Spirit-Type Monster?"

07:40.980 --> 07:42.810
Excuse me!

07:42.810 --> 07:44.970
If you've come here,

07:44.970 --> 07:47.520
you must be seeking the 
power of the spirits.

07:50.360 --> 07:55.160
Hmph. Well, you seem to have 
some degree of competence.

07:55.160 --> 07:56.580
Wait here.

07:58.540 --> 08:01.000
Quest: "Three Trials"

07:58.540 --> 08:01.000
Conditions for Completion

07:58.540 --> 08:01.000
Boost the three designated items to max strength, and turn them in with the abilities specified.

07:59.140 --> 08:01.000
"Three Trials."

08:01.000 --> 08:04.870
"Boost the three designated 
items to max strength,

08:04.870 --> 08:09.080
and turn them in with the 
abilities specified."

08:09.080 --> 08:10.770
That seems pretty hard.

08:10.770 --> 08:13.970
Here. These are the 
instructions for making it.

08:14.340 --> 08:17.930
Oh, dear. These are all items 
I've never seen before.

08:17.930 --> 08:20.620
The spirits are fickle beings.

08:20.620 --> 08:24.550
With their help, you can make 
something truly fantastic,

08:24.550 --> 08:28.200
but you need to be a master 
worthy of their aid.

08:28.200 --> 08:29.420
Okay, got it.

08:29.860 --> 08:31.570
Conditions for Completion

08:29.860 --> 08:31.570
Boost the three designated items to max strength, and turn them in with the abilities specified.

08:32.600 --> 08:36.780
Hmm... These are all 
high-difficulty materials.

08:37.100 --> 08:39.310
Might be hard without a party...

08:39.310 --> 08:40.910
Iz!

08:41.160 --> 08:43.120
Hey!

08:43.120 --> 08:47.320
Oh, hi, Maple. Is your recon going well?

08:47.320 --> 08:50.840
Yeah! Mii invited me to 
go out leveling today.

08:50.840 --> 08:52.590
We were just on our way out.

08:52.590 --> 08:57.110
Oh, really? Then I guess I 
can't ask for your help today.

08:58.850 --> 09:03.430
Ooh! A monster that no one's 
been able to tame yet?

09:03.430 --> 09:07.130
That sounds fascinating. Shall 
the three of us go, then?

09:07.130 --> 09:07.870
Huh?

09:07.870 --> 09:09.420
Are you sure, Mii?

09:09.420 --> 09:12.420
This will take us to a relatively 
challenging area, no?

09:12.420 --> 09:15.490
Which means it should be 
good for leveling. Plus...

09:17.370 --> 09:20.870
It gives me a chance to observe 
a rival guild's abilities.

09:20.870 --> 09:24.510
You're a lifesaver! Can I 
count on you to help, then?

09:24.510 --> 09:26.500
Yeah! Let's go!

09:26.500 --> 09:29.750
That's that, then. Where 
are we headed first?

09:29.750 --> 09:33.340
A volcano. It looks like it's 
pretty far from the city.

09:33.340 --> 09:35.630
Then we can get Syrup to carry us!

09:37.190 --> 09:39.250
I know an even better way.

09:39.250 --> 09:40.570
Leave this to me.

09:40.570 --> 09:42.440
Ignis! [Awaken]!

09:47.970 --> 09:51.400
Ooh! Is that your partner, Mii?

09:51.400 --> 09:53.860
I see! Looks like it's based on a phoenix.

09:53.860 --> 09:56.990
Wow! It's so cool!

09:56.990 --> 09:58.370
Isn't it?

09:58.370 --> 10:00.290
Ignis! [Megamorph]!

10:08.190 --> 10:09.670
It's so fast.

10:09.670 --> 10:11.960
At this pace, we'll be there in no time.

10:14.090 --> 10:15.970
You're pretty fired up, huh?

10:17.260 --> 10:20.890
I-I wanted to show it off right 
away. What do you think?

10:20.890 --> 10:22.610
I think it's awesome!

10:26.770 --> 10:27.640
So this is it?

10:27.640 --> 10:29.940
Leave this to me. I know this place well.

10:30.590 --> 10:32.230
Return, Ignis.

10:34.200 --> 10:37.080
So, um... What is it we need again?

10:37.080 --> 10:39.770
Various ores and plants,

10:39.770 --> 10:42.450
and an item from the boss, the Lava Dragon.

10:42.670 --> 10:46.090
Wow, there are plants in a volcano?

10:46.090 --> 10:49.240
It's a red plant that's 
easy to miss, I believe.

10:49.560 --> 10:51.180
We should remain alert as we search.

10:54.700 --> 10:55.630
There they are!

10:55.630 --> 10:59.090
This one... and this... and this, too.

10:59.470 --> 11:03.180
Monsters could come at us 
from anywhere. Be alert.

11:03.180 --> 11:07.370
Mii, if they're fire-based monsters, you're 
not the best fit against them, are you?

11:07.370 --> 11:08.840
No, I'm not.

11:08.840 --> 11:12.300
But the experience ratio here is very good.

11:12.300 --> 11:14.180
Perfect for leveling, too.

11:18.150 --> 11:20.360
Let's take care of this before more show up!

11:20.360 --> 11:22.300
Ignis! [Linked Flame]!

11:22.300 --> 11:22.990
[Flame]!

11:29.540 --> 11:31.540
You won't top me!

11:31.540 --> 11:33.190
[Loving Sacrifice]!

11:33.190 --> 11:35.000
And Syrup, [Awaken]!

11:35.000 --> 11:37.210
[Deploy Cannon, Right Hand]!

11:37.210 --> 11:39.230
Syrup, [Spirit Cannon]!

11:37.210 --> 11:40.430
Tur...

11:41.050 --> 11:42.180
...tle!

11:42.180 --> 11:43.390
[Hydra]!

11:43.890 --> 11:46.760
[Commence Attack]! Take that!

11:51.060 --> 11:53.400
My firepower is superior!

11:53.400 --> 11:55.310
[Heavy Fire]! [Blue Fire]!

12:01.030 --> 12:03.910
Ooh, <i>such</i> power!

12:03.910 --> 12:05.490
Okay, my turn!

12:13.430 --> 12:15.370
That wasn't half bad.

12:15.370 --> 12:17.610
Not as powerful as your defense, though.

12:17.610 --> 12:19.790
Yeah, true...

12:19.790 --> 12:23.880
I've been using [Hydra] since 
I first started playing.

12:23.880 --> 12:27.880
Well, if you mastered both, 
where would that leave me?

12:27.880 --> 12:30.100
Looks like things have calmed down for now.

12:30.100 --> 12:33.230
Here you go. My own special-made potions.

12:33.230 --> 12:35.060
To thank you, y'know?

12:37.450 --> 12:41.120
Incredible... My MP has fully recovered.

12:41.120 --> 12:44.610
It even boosted the strength 
of my magic attacks.

12:44.990 --> 12:47.640
Should we have used these? 
They must be valuable.

12:47.640 --> 12:49.700
I've never seen such potion effects.

12:49.700 --> 12:54.540
What did I tell you? I made them 
myself, and I can always make more.

12:54.540 --> 12:58.470
Of course. You're a member 
of Maple Tree, too.

12:58.470 --> 13:00.630
That means you're no ordinary player.

13:01.420 --> 13:05.940
I normally play a supporting role, 
so hearing that is new to me.

13:14.390 --> 13:17.440
Will we take damage walking across this?

13:17.440 --> 13:20.210
No, there's no terrain damage here.

13:20.210 --> 13:23.110
The monsters are more powerful, though.

13:25.360 --> 13:26.570
Here it comes!

13:34.650 --> 13:36.020
[Loving Sacrifice]!

13:36.810 --> 13:38.390
[Deploy Armaments]!

13:41.750 --> 13:43.630
Ignis, go!

13:47.560 --> 13:51.000
Here I come, too!

13:51.000 --> 13:52.930
[Invitation to the Ocean Floor]!

13:54.100 --> 13:55.100
Huh?!

13:58.280 --> 13:59.460
Take that!

14:00.810 --> 14:02.140
Huh?!

14:02.140 --> 14:04.020
Ah, a skill that works with [Devour]!

14:04.020 --> 14:08.200
Amazing, Maple! Shame 
it's not cute, though...

14:08.200 --> 14:09.870
Maple, one more blow!

14:09.870 --> 14:11.030
[Inferno]!

14:14.620 --> 14:16.350
That won't work!

14:19.960 --> 14:21.050
In that case...

14:22.280 --> 14:25.080
Ah, my magic increased even more?

14:25.080 --> 14:27.860
My turn, then! [Magic Boost]!

14:28.590 --> 14:30.510
Ignis! Go for it!

14:45.360 --> 14:47.760
Ignis! [Linked Flame]!

14:47.760 --> 14:49.070
[Flame]!

14:54.450 --> 14:56.810
Ignis! [Holy Phoenix Flame]!

14:56.810 --> 14:57.950
[Crimson Flame]!

15:00.280 --> 15:01.890
And this ends it!

15:01.890 --> 15:03.590
[Heavy Fire]! [Blue Fire]!

15:12.430 --> 15:16.100
Thanks so much, both of 
you! Let me go get that!

15:16.830 --> 15:19.710
That was all thanks to you, 
Mii! You were awesome!

15:20.280 --> 15:23.310
Forget that right now! What 
were those tentacles?!

15:24.790 --> 15:27.780
I told you I had something 
to show you, remember?

15:27.780 --> 15:31.800
You did, but how was I 
supposed to expect <i>that</i>?

15:31.800 --> 15:36.120
I wanted to try it on a boss! 
Think it'd make a good finisher?

15:36.120 --> 15:37.740
Definitely.

15:37.740 --> 15:43.490
Jeez, I was afraid you had a shortage 
of firepower, but I guess not.

15:43.950 --> 15:45.880
I'll have to think about

15:45.880 --> 15:48.840
what I can do to counter you in time 
for the next guild competition.

15:50.070 --> 15:51.640
I'll take you anytime!

15:51.640 --> 15:56.140
And all the members of Maple Tree 
have gotten a lot stronger, too.

15:56.140 --> 15:58.970
I bet. I just got a taste of it.

15:59.380 --> 16:03.590
I didn't think Maple Tree had 
a really powerful buffer,

16:03.590 --> 16:05.440
but I was wrong.

16:05.690 --> 16:08.830
In fact, I'd say you guys are unrivaled.

16:08.830 --> 16:12.400
Right? Iz really comes through for us!

16:14.010 --> 16:17.100
All right, what else do you need?

16:17.100 --> 16:19.830
The egg of a monster bird 
that nests on a cliff,

16:19.830 --> 16:21.990
an Ice Flower from the snowy mountains,

16:21.990 --> 16:25.960
venom from a scorpion that lives 
among coral in the ocean...

16:26.180 --> 16:28.130
There's some kind of hide, too.

16:28.130 --> 16:30.090
That all sounds pretty intense.

16:30.090 --> 16:33.170
All right, let's visit each of those places.

16:33.170 --> 16:36.500
I appreciate it! Can we 
start with the cliff, then?

16:36.500 --> 16:38.620
Got it. Leave it to me!

16:46.450 --> 16:48.760
This sure is a long quest.

16:50.030 --> 16:52.740
I've been to ten places already.

16:53.180 --> 16:55.590
I've gotta be near the end by now...

17:05.460 --> 17:07.920
Looks like a little horror-themed area.

17:08.760 --> 17:13.990
I should be able to get a pretty strong 
monster from a quest this long.

17:14.850 --> 17:19.700
A ghost or undead monster would 
probably scare Sally, though.

17:19.700 --> 17:23.020
Uh-oh. They really are that type, huh?

17:33.630 --> 17:36.030
Ah, looks like we've got a new one.

17:36.420 --> 17:37.530
[Revitalize]!

17:38.110 --> 17:39.670
[Shield Attack]!

17:46.060 --> 17:49.400
I can't die as long as 
[Revitalize] is active!

17:51.500 --> 17:55.300
I've been after a kind of durability 
that's different from Maple's.

17:55.910 --> 17:59.640
But if I just keep coming 
back every time I die...

17:59.640 --> 18:03.020
I'm basically just like a zombie.

18:07.970 --> 18:09.940
This must be the boss room.

18:13.220 --> 18:14.570
[Guard Aura]!

18:16.930 --> 18:20.820
Okay, let's find out which one 
of us can hold out longer!

18:34.800 --> 18:35.940
[Flame Slash]!

18:49.600 --> 18:52.050
That went quicker than I thought it would.

18:52.440 --> 18:56.870
But I can at least expect to find 
some kind of treasure here, right?

19:04.020 --> 19:06.490
Ah... This is nice to see,

19:06.830 --> 19:09.210
but surely this isn't all I get.

19:13.220 --> 19:15.170
Hmm, what's this?

19:15.170 --> 19:17.470
Guess I can put it on and see.

19:23.470 --> 19:26.510
Are you the tame monster 
that comes with this ring?

19:27.020 --> 19:28.350
Let's see...

19:29.090 --> 19:30.730
[Armored]?

19:43.490 --> 19:47.960
Well done. The spirits 
will surely aid you now.

19:51.410 --> 19:54.310
Here. Put this on your finger,

19:54.310 --> 19:56.360
and go stand on that circle.

20:09.970 --> 20:12.150
That is a spirit.

20:12.150 --> 20:15.310
Their powers differ depending 
on where they are found.

20:15.310 --> 20:19.690
Use the terrain and magic skillfully 
to control those powers.

20:19.910 --> 20:23.660
Huh... I guess it's similar 
to elemental magic?

20:24.290 --> 20:27.130
Nice to meet you. My name's Iz.

20:27.130 --> 20:31.120
I'm going to call you "Fay." 
I hope we'll be good friends.

20:31.120 --> 20:32.380
Fay?

20:33.420 --> 20:35.580
Congratulations!

20:35.580 --> 20:40.090
I've made a wonderful little 
friend thanks to you and Mii.

20:40.620 --> 20:43.100
My Sou is really cool, too.

20:43.100 --> 20:47.550
I'll keep its skills a secret 
until the next event, though.

20:47.550 --> 20:49.180
We'll look forward to it!

20:49.180 --> 20:52.770
What about you, Kuromu? What 
kind of monster did you find?

20:52.770 --> 20:55.320
Oh, check this out. Necro!

20:59.210 --> 21:02.400
Sorry, Sally. Just try to get used to it.

21:02.400 --> 21:05.990
This is my partner. Its name is Necro.

21:05.990 --> 21:09.830
N-No... Yeah, I'm okay.

21:10.490 --> 21:15.710
The armor is, uh... pretty 
cool-looking, at least.

21:15.710 --> 21:19.150
Yeah? Then let me show you what it can do!

21:19.580 --> 21:20.670
[Armored]!

21:41.320 --> 21:43.900
Yeah, uh...

21:46.550 --> 21:48.570
You look so cool, Kuromu!

21:49.420 --> 21:50.930
I know, right?!

21:50.930 --> 21:53.660
This gives me even more durability, too.

21:53.660 --> 21:56.130
It's the best partner I could ask for!

21:56.130 --> 21:58.080
Glad to know ya, Necro!

21:58.080 --> 22:00.660
Kuromu, I want to see that again!

21:59.210 --> 22:00.660
Boys...

22:00.660 --> 22:02.000
Me, too!

22:00.660 --> 22:02.000
Fay.

22:02.000 --> 22:10.010
< [NWO] Level 7, Thread 8: Tame Monsters "Way to go, admins! Well done!"

22:02.190 --> 22:06.050
Everyone in Maple Tree's got their partners now

22:02.570 --> 22:06.050
I saw on the bulletin boards that they're all rare ones

22:03.320 --> 22:06.050
Figures

22:04.110 --> 22:06.050
Seems like they all took a lot of time and effort to find.
 I'm impressed

22:05.030 --> 22:06.050
Think anyone else could get the same monsters they have?

22:06.050 --> 22:06.580
Everyone in Maple Tree's got their partners now

22:06.050 --> 22:06.590
